# Wiktionary contribution tooling (tools/wiktionary).
# The records/ directory is deliberately NOT ignored - it is the audit trail of
# every edit the tool has made.
tools/wiktionary/.venv/
tools/wiktionary/user-config.py
tools/wiktionary/user-password.py
tools/wiktionary/*.lwp
tools/wiktionary/work/

# Pywikibot's own scratch, written into PYWIKIBOT_DIR
tools/wiktionary/apicache/
tools/wiktionary/logs/
tools/wiktionary/throttle.ctrl
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.DS_Store

# Prerendered pages, written by build/lib/prerender.mjs on every build: ~6,280
# HTML files, about 66 MB. Generated, so not committed - Cloudflare Pages runs
# `npm run build` and writes them at deploy time. The shell they are built from,
# public/index.html, IS committed, and so is everything else at the top level.
#
# Two depths, because there are two shapes: a word is /gba/take/index.html and a
# written page is /about/index.html. Ignoring only the deeper one meant About,
# Contribute and the other four would have been committed.
/public/*/index.html
/public/*/*/index.html
/public/*/*/*/index.html
/public/sitemap.xml
/public/_redirects
/public/data/version.json

# tools/slugs work: the review worksheets, one per letter. Generated from the
# ledger, edited by hand, read back, and then disposable. data/url-slugs.json is
# the committed artifact - that one is the point.
tools/slugs/work/
tools/slugs/.venv/
